{"v": 3, "date": "2026-11-19", "title": "Snow on the peaks Sunday 22 November, then a cold signal around Thursday 10 December: what to expect in the coming weeks", "lead": ["For the next few days the high-resolution models lead: they see snowfall Sunday 22 November, about 40 cm at Monte Prado (2054 m). It's a short episode, to be confirmed in the next updates.", "Beyond that episode no serious snow for now, but some scenarios bring cold air around Thursday 10 December: that's the signal to watch in the next updates.", "We combined 297 scenarios from 8 different weather models, up to Friday 18 December.", "🥶 Real cold is coming: from Thursday 26 November the air is cold enough for snow down to the resorts"], "phases": [{"emoji": "🌧️", "label": "Next 5 days", "text": "From Thu 19 to Mon 23: mostly Rain (41 scenarios out of 100). Snow: very unlikely (2 out of 100). Typical temperature at altitude around +6 °C, reliability medium. No model gives snow in at least 30 scenarios out of 100. The coarse-grid global models miss the snowfall on the peaks on Sunday 22 November that the high-resolution ones see: in these cases trust the local forecast.", "color": "#94a3b8"}, {"emoji": "🌧️", "label": "Days 6 to 10", "text": "From Tue 24 to Sat 28: mostly Rain (39 scenarios out of 100). Snow: unlikely (18 out of 100). Typical temperature at altitude around +4 °C, reliability medium. No model gives snow in at least 30 scenarios out of 100. The most promising day for snow is Thursday 26 November. Watch out for the cold: in 11 scenarios out of 100 it drops below −2 °C at 1500 m (the coldest down to -5 °C), especially around Thursday 26 November.", "color": "#94a3b8"}, {"emoji": "☀️", "label": "Days 11 to 15", "text": "From Sun 29 to Thu 3: mostly Dry and mild (34 scenarios out of 100). Snow: unlikely (10 out of 100). Typical temperature at altitude around +5 °C, reliability medium. No model gives snow in at least 30 scenarios out of 100.", "color": "#fbbf24"}, {"emoji": "🌧️", "label": "Days 16 to 30", "text": "From Fri 4 to Fri 18: mostly Rain (32 scenarios out of 100). Snow: unlikely (14 out of 100). Typical temperature at altitude around +3 °C, reliability low. No model gives snow in at least 30 scenarios out of 100. The most promising day for snow is Thursday 17 December. Watch out for the cold: in 21 scenarios out of 100 it drops below −2 °C at 1500 m (the coldest down to -5 °C), especially around Thursday 10 December.", "color": "#94a3b8"}], "models": ["Between Tue 24 and Sat 28 the most convinced model is UK Met Office (29 snowy scenarios out of 100), the most sceptical GEM (8).", "The models broadly agree: a signal worth taking seriously."], "pros": ["Our estimate of the snow level on the ridge on days with precipitation: Thu 2900 m, Sun 2200 m, Mon 1400 m.", "The most interesting day is Mon: with snow around 1400 m the resorts turn white too."], "big": ["The big picture points towards cold: the next model runs could add snow.", "NAO near zero in the second week: no clear push towards cold or towards high pressure (17 negative, 21 positive scenarios out of 100).", "Arctic Oscillation dropping sharply: polar cold air tends to slide towards mid-latitudes, Europe included.", "Sudden stratospheric warming: around Tuesday 10 November the stratospheric winds along 60°N reversed, from westerly to easterly (minimum -3 m/s); the vortex is now rebuilding (about 38 m/s around Friday 4 December). After such events the odds of cold air reaching Europe rise over the following 2–4 weeks: the window to watch runs from Tuesday 24 November to Tuesday 8 December. It raises the odds, it doesn't guarantee anything."], "weekend": ["Saturday: Good weather pretty much everywhere: pick the handiest spot.", "Sunday: Fresh snow only on the peaks, more or less everywhere: little or none lower down."], "ground": "For now the official stations measure no significant snow on the ground.", "chart": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 900 250\" class=\"syn-chart\" role=\"img\" aria-labe